 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Mathlib defines `def interedges ... := {e \u2208 s \u00d7\u02e2 t | r e.1 e.2}` (Density.lean:46) and `def edgeDensity ... := #(interedges r s t) / (#s * #t)` (Density.lean:49). The sibling adapters in PairColor/Graph.lean:83-85 rewrite with `SimpleGraph.edgeDensity_def, SimpleGraph.interedges_def` and then use `simp`, not `rfl`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Combinatorics/Hypergraph/PairColor/Density.lean",
   "fix": "Unfold explicitly with `rw [Rel.edgeDensity, Rel.interedges]` (or `simp only [...]`) before closing. If an instance mismatch still needs `rfl` or `convert`, add a comment saying so.",
   "issue": "After the `rw`, the bare `rfl` silently unfolds `Rel.edgeDensity` and `Rel.interedges` and lines up the classical filter-decidability instance. This is defeq across a Mathlib wrapper with no comment, so it breaks if Mathlib changes either definition.",
   "line": 86
  }
 ],
